---
Find the smallest population circle for one registered country

Usage: popcircles country smallest [OPTIONS] --country <COUNTRY> --share <SHARE>

Options:
      --country <COUNTRY>          Exact country feature identifier or unique English name
      --log-level <LEVEL>          How much to report on stderr: `error`, `warn`, `info` or `debug`. It does not govern the progress meter, which answers how far a run has got rather than what happened [default: info]
      --config <PATH>              Optional configuration file layered over data/config.toml
      --share <SHARE>              The share of this country's population to reach, in whole percent
      --combination <COMBINATION>  Configured population and boundary sources to query
      --resolution <RESOLUTION>    Prepared resolution; defaults to the combination's configured default
      --spacing <SPACING>          Override the initial block side in cells, derived from each radius and the grid when omitted. Changes runtime only; the answer is the same at every spacing
      --ledger <LEDGER>            Country-specific resume ledger. Defaults to `out/countries/<ID>.json`
  -h, --help                       Print help
